{ Hello everyone! 😃

This study is about.....🥁🥁🥁
🛸 The Alien and Martian Gambits! 👽

These are very risky but very rewarding gambits (invented (to my knowledge) by a guy with a username in some places as WittyAlien): so stockfish 🐟 does not like them.

Thankfully, your opponents (hopefully) won't be using stockfish, so they will have to solve their problems with their human brain.

This is mostly structured using our opponents most common moves, and the commoner ones first (usually).

Before you begin the study, please like the study by clicking the heart button down there. ⬇ I worked hard on this study, and doing so helps support the study.

Also, join these cool teams: https://lichess.org/team/study-resource-team https://lichess.org/team/study-creators--friends

Thanks! }
 *


[Event "The Alien and Martian Gambits: 🛸 Alien Gambit 7. ...Bg4??"]
[Date "2025.08.27"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "B15"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Alien Gambit"]
[StudyName "The Alien and Martian Gambits"]
[ChapterName "🛸 Alien Gambit 7. ...Bg4??"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/tU7Nq5nE/fAdjmWvM"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/FlamingHawk3000"]
[UTCDate "2025.08.27"]
[UTCTime "01:12:58"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ [%csl Ge4][%cal Ge2e4] }
1. e4 c6 { The Caro-Kann defense, known to be solid. 🪨 But let's rip it apart! Play d4! } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd2d4] } 2. d4 d5 { Black strikes in the center attacks our e-pawn. How can we defend our pawn? } { [%csl Re4][%cal Rd5e4] } 3. Nc3 { [%csl Re4][%cal Rc3e4] } 3... dxe4 { This is the mainline, played 76% of the time. I'll show you how to beat the side lines later. 😉 } 4. Nxe4 Nf6 { We will start we the Alien gambit. Black offers a trade of knights. He wants us to take a solidify his kingside, and simplify into a comfortable endgame.
Can we target f7?🎯 } { [%csl Rf7] } 5. Ng5 { Attacking f7. You may ask, "How are we attacking f7?"🤔
You will see. 😏 } { [%csl Rf7][%cal Rg5f7] } 5... h6 { Played 55% of the time. Playing exactly into our hand. We could move our knight back, or we could... } { [%csl Rf7] } 6. Nxf7 { SAC THE KNIGHT!!!
We have LASTING POSTIONAL and TACTICAL COMPENSATION. We are not FULLY compensated, but that is the nature of a gambit. 😉 } { [%csl Be7,Be6,Bg6,Bf7,Re8][%cal Gg1f3,Gf1d3] } 6... Kxf7 { The only move. Now we may be tempted to go after the king immediately with Bc4+, but it is instead better to build up before going for the kill.
Can you find a quiet developing move? } 7. Nf3 Bg4 { The most played move. Black develops, and seemingly stops the knight from moving. But, surprisingly, after this move its all over. 😀 How can you win. } 8. Ne5+ { [%csl Rg4,Rf7][%cal Re5g4,Re5f7] } 8... Kg8 { We could take the bishop, but its better to throw in a check first.😉 } 9. Bc4+ { We are still winning the bishop. } { [%csl Rg4][%cal Re5g4,Rd1g4] } 9... Kh7 { After this move played 42% of the time, its truly, very over. If e6, we can just take the bishop, and we have an extra pawn and an exceedingly safer king.👍How can you win on the spot? } 10. Qd3+ { All black can do is block and hope white mouse-slips. } 10... Ne4 { Just keep getting closer to the king. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gd3e4] } 11. Qxe4+ Bf5 { [%csl Gf5][%cal Ge4f5] } 12. Qxf5+ g6 { Get ready for it, and... } { [%csl Gg6][%cal Gf5g6] } 13. Qxg6# { Checkmate. And in 13 moves! Great job!😄 } *


