{ Now our opponent will play....... will play........ (click the space bar...... 😆😉) }
7... Nbd7 { Nbd7! Can you remember our battle plan? } 8. Bd3 { Yes! Great job! } 8... e6 { Continue the plan. 😉😃👍 } 9. O-O Bd6 { Ok with the knight on d7 do not play Ne5 yet! We need to prepare it with our..... (Rook) } { [%csl Re5][%cal Rd7e5,Rd6e5,Rd4e5] } 10. Re1 { Rook! We are ready to blow up the battlefield! } { [%csl Re5][%cal Re1e5] } 10... Re8 { Big mistake! Now charge!!!! } 11. Ne5+ { If black takes we take back almost +2 and just win. However, if black is smart... } 11... Kg8 { They retreat! Develop our queen! } 12. Qf3 Qc7 { Now how can we prepare to take on h6? } { [%csl Rh6,Rg8][%cal Rc1h6] } 13. Qg3 { Pin the pawn! } 13... Nf8 { Under pressure, black makes a critical mistake, which is, of course, most played. } 14. Bxh6 { Yum yum! 😏🍴 I bet next move black will make a most played mistake. } 14... Bxe5 { Mistake. Most played. It happens again! (That wasn't exactly fair... but still. 😉) } 15. dxe5 { Yum yum! } 15... Nd5 { Most played mistake. How can you rook lift? } { [%csl Re1] } 16. Re4 { Nice. I'll stop here. White has an overwhelming attack, and is +2.5 ahead. Great job! 😃 (75% win rate 😉) } *


