[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Please remember to like the study if you're enjoying it so far! Ok, now let's move on to the Martian gambit sections. Play e4! 😃 } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Ge2e4] }
1. e4 c6 { You know what to do. 😉 } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd2d4] } 2. d4 d5 { Now defend our pawn. } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gb1c3] } 3. Nc3 dxe4 { We recapture. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gc3e4] } 4. Nxe4 Bf5 { This move will lead to... 🥁 The Martian Gambit! 😃 How can we do pretty much the same thing as last time? } 5. Ng5 { We advance our horsey. } { [%csl Rf7,Re6][%cal Rg5f7,Rg5e6] } 5... Bg6 { Oh know! Black is defending f7? What do we do? Just develop for now... 😉😏 } 6. N1f3 { We develop the horsey and prepare an annoying move... } 6... h6 { Black kick our knight! We could bring it back but where could we plop it instead? 🤔 Think outside of the 📦. } 7. Ne6 { Brilliant!!!! THE MARTIAN GAMBIT!!!! This is probably the favorite of the two gambits. } 7... fxe6 { Black accepts our "free" knight. We have nothing yet, but soon we can get our revenge... How can we kick annoying Mr. Bishop? } { [%csl Rg6] } 8. Ne5 { Nice. Good kicking. } 8... Bf7 { Most common but an.... inaccuracy. How can we develop this bishop to an optimal diagonal? } { [%csl Rf1] } 9. Bc4 Nf6 { Black stops (for now) any Bxe6!! Bxe6 Qh5+! nonsense. Where is the best spot for our queen? } { [%csl Rd1] } 10. Qd3 { On d3, eyeing the weak light squares! 😃 } { [%csl Rg6,Rf5,Re6,Rf7,Re8,Rd7] } 10... Nbd7 { Fill in the blank: The most ________ move and a big _________. (Answer key: common, mistake.) Just munch on black's best defender. } 11. Nxf7 Kxf7 { Noooooo!!!! 😱 Our last kinght. 😢😭 How can we find the MOST BRILLIANT MOVE EVER!!! Hint: eye the light squares. } { [%csl Rd3] } 12. Qf5 { So awesome!!!!!! 🤯😱😲 The pin saves us!!! Here most people (almost all) die very, very quickly. } { [%csl Rf7][%cal Rc4f7] } 12... Ke8 { The most common move. Hint: Look for CHECKMATE!!!!!! } 13. Qg6# { Checkmate on the light squares. How did I see that coming? Great job! 😃 } *


